# The Short S.23 Empire flying boat, Imperial Airways' C class of 1936:
# JSBSim's model, with its hull's and floats' hydrodynamics, held to Short
# Brothers' and Flight's figures (assets/figures/short_s23.xml). It stands on
# water, and takes off from and alights on it.

name Short S.23 Empire Flying Boat
model short_s23
class seaplane
start 130 0.5
# Her de Havilland two-pitch airscrews: fine for take-off and climb, coarse
# for cruise, as Flight's figures fly her (assets/figures/short_s23.xml: the
# climb at 100 kt in fine pitch, the 200 mph level speed in coarse). An
# airborne start faster than her climbing speed, 100 kt, is in coarse; her
# book gives no other speed between, so the climb's is the line.
airscrew-coarse-above 100
# Her mixture: the Claudel-Hobson A.V.T. 85E carburettor's automatic
# mixture control, its lever rich for take-off (with the take-off boost) and
# set back for the climb and cruise ("Take-off, 1:10; Rated, 1:11; Normal
# Cruising, 1:12", CAB 1943, in engines.xml). Rich below her engines' rated
# altitude, 4,500 ft (Flight, 12 November 1936, in eng_PegasusXc.xml), and
# above it set for the most power, as the autopilot leans.
mixture-lever 4500
seaplane
